{
  "changeName": "pc-301",
  "changeDir": "/work/openspec/changes/pc-301",
  "schemaName": "spec-driven",
  "contextFiles": {
    "proposal": [
      "/work/openspec/changes/pc-301/proposal.md"
    ],
    "specs": [
      "/work/openspec/changes/pc-301/specs/owner-details/spec.md",
      "/work/openspec/changes/pc-301/specs/pets/spec.md"
    ],
    "design": [
      "/work/openspec/changes/pc-301/design.md"
    ],
    "tasks": [
      "/work/openspec/changes/pc-301/tasks.md"
    ]
  },
  "progress": {
    "total": 21,
    "complete": 0,
    "remaining": 21
  },
  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "1",
      "description": "0.1 Give the pet inserts in `db/h2/data.sql` and `db/mysql/data.sql` a column list (`id, name, birth_date, type_id, owner_id`), because they insert by position today (`db/h2/data.sql:36-48`, `db/mysql/data.sql:36-48`). Change nothing else: no schema change, no migration script, no microchip number. Leave `db/postgres/data.sql` unchanged: it already names its columns. Verify: the app starts on H2, `./mvnw test` passes with no failures beyond those noted at the baseline, and the release-1 diff touches only those two files. Where Docker is available, also run `MySqlIntegrationTests`; without Docker it is skipped, so report it as not run.",
      "done": false,
      "sourcePath": "/work/openspec/changes/pc-301/tasks.md",
      "line": 9
    },
    {
      "id": "2",
      "description": "0.2 Release 1 is merged and released on its own, before any task of release 2 is merged. Deployment step 1 of design Decision 8 (release 1 deployed, no older instance left) must be done before the migration script runs on any database.",
      "done": false,
      "sourcePath": "/work/openspec/changes/pc-301/tasks.md",
      "line": 10
    },
    {
      "id": "3",
      "description": "1.1 Add the nullable `microchip_number` column and the constraint `unique_pet_microchip_number` to `db/h2/schema.sql`, `db/mysql/schema.sql` and `db/postgres/schema.sql`, as in design Decisions 1 and 5. The seed inserts already name their columns (task 0.1). No seeded pet gets a microchip number (F8). Verify: the app starts on H2 and `./mvnw test -Dtest=ClinicServiceTests` passes.",
      "done": false,
      "sourcePath": "/work/openspec/changes/pc-301/tasks.md",
      "line": 18
    },
    {
      "id": "4",
      "description": "1.2 Add `microchipNumber` to `Pet`, with the normalising setter from design Decision 2 (trim, remove spaces, empty becomes `null`). Verify: new unit tests in `PetTests` or `OwnerTests` show that `\" 985 141 000 123 456 \"` becomes `\"985141000123456\"`, that `\"   \"` and `\"\"` become `null`, and that `\"985-141-000-123-456\"` is kept as it is. Run them with `./mvnw test -Dtest=OwnerTests` (or the new class).",
      "done": false,
      "sourcePath": "/work/openspec/changes/pc-301/tasks.md",
      "line": 19
    },
    {
      "id": "5",
      "description": "1.3 Add `PetRepository` with `existsByMicrochipNumber` and `existsByMicrochipNumberAndIdNot`. Verify: a test against H2 in `ClinicServiceTests` shows that both queries find another pet's number, that `existsByMicrochipNumberAndIdNot` does not find the pet's own number, and that two pets with no number can be saved. This covers the scenario \"Two pets without a microchip number\".",
      "done": false,
      "sourcePath": "/work/openspec/changes/pc-301/tasks.md",
      "line": 20
    },
    {
      "id": "6",
      "description": "1.4 Add a deterministic test of the database duplicate on H2 to `ClinicServiceTests`, modelled on `shouldFailToInsertDuplicatePetNameForSameOwner` (`ClinicServiceTests.java:253-277`). It saves two pets, for different owners, with the same microchip number through `OwnerRepository.saveAndFlush`, so `PetValidator` does not run. It asserts that the save throws `DataIntegrityViolationException` and that the exception's message contains `unique_pet_microchip_number`, ignoring case. This is the only test that reads H2's real message: the race test (task 4.2) may never reach the `catch` (design, Risks). Verify: `./mvnw test -Dtest=ClinicServiceTests` passes.",
      "done": false,
      "sourcePath": "/work/openspec/changes/pc-301/tasks.md",
      "line": 21
    },
    {
      "id": "7",
      "description": "1.5 Add the migration scripts of design Decision 8 (D23): `src/main/resources/db/mysql/migrate-pc-301-microchip-number.sql` and `src/main/resources/db/postgres/migrate-pc-301-microchip-number.sql`, each adding the nullable column first and the constraint `unique_pet_microchip_number` second, with a leading comment that says to run it after release 1 is deployed and before release 2 is (D25). None for H2. Add one migration test per database, following the existing patterns and adding no dependency to `pom.xml` (D26, F13): the MySQL test uses a `testcontainers-mysql` container with `@Testcontainers(disabledWithoutDocker = true)`, as `MySqlIntegrationTests.java:43-49` does; the Postgres test starts Postgres through Spring Boot's Docker Compose support and skips itself without Docker, as `PostgresIntegrationTests.java:51-52,68` does. If either test cannot be written without a new dependency, stop and raise it with the ticket owner. Each test creates the `pets` table and the tables it references from the `schema.sql` of release 1 (the same as before this change), kept as a test resource, and inserts a pet. It then runs the migration script and checks that the existing pet has no microchip number, that two pets without a number can be saved, and that a second pet with the same number is rejected with an error that names `unique_pet_microchip_number`, ignoring case. Finally it runs the new `schema.sql` against the migrated database and checks that it succeeds, which is what step 3 of the deployment in Decision 8 relies on. Verify: with Docker, both tests pass. Without Docker they are skipped: report them as not run, not as passed (known gap, D23).",
      "done": false,
      "sourcePath": "/work/openspec/changes/pc-301/tasks.md",
      "line": 22
    },
    {
      "id": "8",
      "description": "2.1 Give `PetValidator` a `PetRepository` constructor argument and add the format check `[0-9]{15}` with code `microchipNumber.invalid`. Verify: `PetValidatorTests` covers 15 digits accepted, `000000000000001` accepted, 14 and 16 digits rejected, `0A0139F53B` rejected, a dashed number rejected, and no number accepted. That is the spec requirements \"Microchip number is optional\", \"is stored as its digits\" and \"is exactly 15 digits\".",
      "done": false,
      "sourcePath": "/work/openspec/changes/pc-301/tasks.md",
      "line": 26
    },
    {
      "id": "9",
      "description": "2.2 Add the uniqueness check with code `duplicate`. It runs only when the format check passes, with `existsByMicrochipNumber` for a new pet and `existsByMicrochipNumberAndIdNot` for an existing one. Verify: `PetValidatorTests`, with a mocked `PetRepository`, covers another pet's number rejected, the pet's own number accepted, and a malformed number that never reaches the repository and gets exactly one error. That is the spec requirements \"unique across all pets\", \"A pet keeps its own microchip number\" and \"One microchip number error at a time\".",
      "done": false,
      "sourcePath": "/work/openspec/changes/pc-301/tasks.md",
      "line": 27
    },
    {
      "id": "10",
      "description": "2.3 Add `microchipNumber` and `microchipNumber.invalid` to `messages.properties` and every `messages_*.properties` except `messages_en`. Verify: `./mvnw test -Dtest=I18nPropertiesSyncTest` passes.",
      "done": false,
      "sourcePath": "/work/openspec/changes/pc-301/tasks.md",
      "line": 28
    },
    {
      "id": "11",
      "description": "3.1 Inject `PetRepository` into `PetController` and build the validator with it in `initPetBinder`. Add `@MockitoBean PetRepository` to `PetControllerTests` and `PetControllerCharacterizationTests`. Verify: both classes pass unchanged otherwise, which shows the baseline `pets` behaviour still holds.",
      "done": false,
      "sourcePath": "/work/openspec/changes/pc-301/tasks.md",
      "line": 32
    },
    {
      "id": "12",
      "description": "3.2 Copy `microchipNumber`, including `null`, in `updatePetDetails`. Verify: new `PetControllerTests` cases for \"A new number replaces the stored one\", \"The field is cleared\" and \"Saving a pet with its own number\" pass. Also check that the existing `editCopiesNameBirthDateAndTypeOntoOwnersPetWhenInstancesDiffer` still passes.",
      "done": false,
      "sourcePath": "/work/openspec/changes/pc-301/tasks.md",
      "line": 33
    },
    {
      "id": "13",
      "description": "3.3 Add the microchip number input to `pets/createOrUpdatePetForm.html`. Verify: `PetControllerTests` asserts that the edit form for a pet with `985141000123456` holds that value and that a pet without a number shows an empty field. `./mvnw test -Dtest=I18nPropertiesSyncTest` still passes.",
      "done": false,
      "sourcePath": "/work/openspec/changes/pc-301/tasks.md",
      "line": 34
    },
    {
      "id": "14",
      "description": "3.4 Verify in `PetControllerTests`:",
      "done": false,
      "sourcePath": "/work/openspec/changes/pc-301/tasks.md",
      "line": 35
    },
    {
      "id": "15",
      "description": "3.5 Add the G3 test (D21): one `@SpringBootTest` on H2 that goes through the forms. It adds a pet with \"985141000123456\", edits it to \"985141000654321\", then clears it. After each step it reads the stored value from the database: \"985141000123456\", then \"985141000654321\", then no number. It also submits an edit with \"12345\" for a pet that has a number, and checks that the form is shown again with \"must be 15 digits\" and that the stored value is unchanged. This covers \"A new number replaces the stored one\", \"The field is cleared\" and \"A malformed new number is rejected\" against a real database, and the detached-entity claim in design Decision 4. Verify: the test passes with `./mvnw test -Dtest=<the new class>`.",
      "done": false,
      "sourcePath": "/work/openspec/changes/pc-301/tasks.md",
      "line": 40
    },
    {
      "id": "16",
      "description": "4.1 Add the `PetValidator` method from design Decision 5 (D19), which rejects `microchipNumber` with the code `duplicate`. In both POST handlers, when a `DataIntegrityViolationException` names `unique_pet_microchip_number` (ignoring case), call that method before the name check and show the form again. Add no `rejectValue` call to `PetController`. Verify: a `PetValidatorTests` case shows that the method puts exactly one error, `duplicate`, on `microchipNumber`. New `PetControllerTests` cases for \"The constraint is reported as a duplicate microchip number\" and \"The name constraint is still reported on the name\" pass, and `createOtherIntegrityViolationIsRethrown` still passes (the MODIFIED scenario \"Another integrity violation\").",
      "done": false,
      "sourcePath": "/work/openspec/changes/pc-301/tasks.md",
      "line": 44
    },
    {
      "id": "17",
      "description": "4.2 Add a race test for two simultaneous adds, for different owners, with the same microchip number to `PetClinicConcurrencyTests`, modelled on `testDuplicatePetNameRaceConditionIsBlocked`. Unlike that template, which counts any non-2xx response or exception as a failure (`PetClinicConcurrencyTests.java:86-95`), assert that the losing request gets the form again (status 200) with \"is already in use\" on the microchip number. Verify: exactly one pet with the number is saved on H2, and the losing response carries that error. The response is the same whether the validator or the database `catch` rejected the losing request, so this test does not show that H2's real message is recognised; task 1.4 does. Where Docker is available, also run `MySqlIntegrationTests` and `PostgresIntegrationTests`. If Docker is missing they are skipped, so report them as not run rather than as passed. They do not test the microchip constraint through the forms either way (known gap recorded with D20, design Risks).",
      "done": false,
      "sourcePath": "/work/openspec/changes/pc-301/tasks.md",
      "line": 45
    },
    {
      "id": "18",
      "description": "4.3 Run `./mvnw test -Dtest=ArchitectureTests`. Verify: it passes with the freeze store unchanged. If it fails, do not edit or regenerate `src/test/resources/archunit_store/`. Stop and raise it with the ticket owner (design Decision 5).",
      "done": false,
      "sourcePath": "/work/openspec/changes/pc-301/tasks.md",
      "line": 46
    },
    {
      "id": "19",
      "description": "5.1 Add the \"Microchip number\" label and value to `owners/ownerDetails.html`, after the type. Verify: `OwnerControllerTests` asserts the label with `985141000123456` for a pet with a number, and the label with an empty value (not \"none\") for a pet without one. That is the spec `owner-details`.",
      "done": false,
      "sourcePath": "/work/openspec/changes/pc-301/tasks.md",
      "line": 50
    },
    {
      "id": "20",
      "description": "6.1 Run `./mvnw spring-javaformat:apply` and then the full `./mvnw test`. Verify: the build passes, and no failures appear beyond those noted at the baseline.",
      "done": false,
      "sourcePath": "/work/openspec/changes/pc-301/tasks.md",
      "line": 54
    },
    {
      "id": "21",
      "description": "6.2 Run `openspec validate pc-301 --strict`. Verify: it reports the change as valid.",
      "done": false,
      "sourcePath": "/work/openspec/changes/pc-301/tasks.md",
      "line": 55
    }
  ],
  "taskTrackingConfigured": true,
  "state": "ready",
  "instruction": "Read context files, work through pending tasks, mark complete as you go.\nPause if you hit blockers or need clarification.",
  "root": {
    "path": "/work",
    "source": "nearest"
  }
}

